  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThe upper ridge axis will shift eastward through next weekend as \na large trough across the western US makes slow progress closer to\nthe area. Showers and a few thunderstorms could make it into \nwestern parts of the area on Saturday but the majority of this \nactivity will be focused to our west across NM into the \npanhandles. \n\nTroughing is then forecasted to weaken and lift northward later \nin the weekend with model disagreement increasing thereafter on \nwhether we see ridging return to the region or additional \ntroughing develop across the southwest US. Either way, it appears \nthe above normal temperatures will continue at least into early \nnext week with highs in the 70s and 80s across the area. \n\nWare",
